        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">Absolutely. Yards with natural slopes, common in areas around Lake Texoma and throughout Denison, are often ideal for concrete storm shelter installations. The slope can facilitate easier access and drainage. Our experts will assess your specific yard's topography to recommend the best and safest placement.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:8px;padding:24px 28px;">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 10px;">What are the common local building codes or permits needed for storm shelter installation in Denison, TX?</h3>
        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:#555;margin:0;">While storm shelters are primarily life-safety devices, local building codes in Denison may require specific permits, especially for new construction or significant modifications. Texoma Storm Shelters is knowledgeable about local regulations and can guide you through any necessary permitting processes to ensure your installation is fully compliant.</p>
      </div>
